    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\n[scikit-learn report this](https://github.com/scikit-learn/scikit-learn/issues/34525).\n\nIf you wrap a cyfunction in a wrapper function, then the wrapper function `__annotate__` is set to the result of `wrapped.__annotate__`, and this can't be reloaded.\n\nIt gives the slightly misleading error message `AttributeError: 'dict' object has no attribute '__annotate__'`.\n\nEssentially the gist is that we create an method with `self` being the annotations dict named `__annotate__`. `__reduce__` for a method object is defined as returning `(__builtins.getattr, (self.__self__, self.__name__))` so when it unpickles it tries to call `getattr(dict, \"__annotate__\")`\n\n### Code to reproduce the behaviour:\n\nSee https://github.com/lesteve/scikit-learn-34525-cython-reproducer for a full example\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\nI think this does need to unpickle cleanly, since wrapped cyfunctions did before (within the ususal limits of cyfunction pickleability).\n\n### OS\n\n_No response_\n\n### Python version\n\n_No response_\n\n### Cython version\n\nmaster, 3.2.6\n\n### Additional context\n\nI think the challenge here is getting something that doesn't add too much extra code. Getting something that works should be possible, but it'd be nice not to have to add extra C classes for this.",
